# Netlify redirects (copied into dist/ by Vite, so they work for Git and drag-and-drop deploys).

# Proxy the API through this site so the browser treats it as same-origin. The backend's
# HTTP-only session cookie then becomes first-party and works in every browser, including
# Safari/iOS, which blocks cross-site cookies. Keep VITE_API_BASE_URL unset in Netlify so the
# app calls the default relative /api/v1.
/api/*  https://wedding-dashboard-be.onrender.com/api/:splat  200!

# SPA fallback: let React Router handle deep links like /dashboard on refresh.
/*  /index.html  200
